  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Heads up – count the fingers",
  "description": "The players pair up with one ball per pair. One dribbles the ball and the other walks backwards in front, holding up a hand with some fingers raised. The dribbler says out loud how many fingers they see. Then the partner shows a new number, and so on. The pairs move up and down the court and swap roles after a while.\n\nBeing able to look up with the ball matters – this is a simple first step. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Feel the ball with the blade and lift your eyes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Short touches so the ball stays close to the stick."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The one showing fingers: change the number often and hold the hand high."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 1,
